            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \varphi(V)_0, \ldots, \varphi(V)_n\rangle
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cov
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cov(X)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSets
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSets
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha,\beta)
            %em do
            get a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagram"} homotopy coherent diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cov
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi SSets
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \check{C}(X,-) : Cov(X)\to SSets.
          %p
            with the coherence being able to be spelled out completely, (see
            = succeed "," do
              %em Coverings, Hypercoverings and Homotopy Coherence
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.maths.bangor.ac.uk/research/ftp/theses/kadir.pdf"} here
          %h3#using_the_vietoris_complex Using the Vietoris complex:
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vietoris+complex"} Vietoris complex
            is an alternative way of obtaining a simplicial complex (or simplicial set) from a space
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and an open cover
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            %em all
            open covers by that of
            %em finite open covers
            without changing the result up to isomorphism), the Vietoris complex has as many vertices as there are points in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Cov
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(X,-) : Cov(X)\to SSet
            %span.newWikiWord
              pro-homotopy type
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/pro-homotopy+type"} ?
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(X)
            in the homotopy category
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi pro
                    %mo −
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(pro-SSet)
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pro
                  %mo −
                  %mi SSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pro-SSet
            has various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration+category"} cofibration category
            structures, with related basic notions of homotopy equivalence. These are discussed in the entry on
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-homotopy+theory"} pro-homotopy theory
          %p How are the two ways around the coherence problem related?
          %p
            There is a result
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dowker%27s+Theorem"} Dowker's Theorem
            which shows that the geometric realisations of
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(X,\alpha)
            and
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \check{C}(X,\alpha)
            are homotopy equivalent. (This explains why Čech and Vietoris homology are isomorphic.) Given a commutative diagram of spaces (or simplicial sets), if you change some of the spaces to homotopy equivalent spaces then you can build from those new spaces, a homotopy coherent diagram equivalent to the original one. Using Dowker’s theorem we get that
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \check{C}(X,-)
            is a homotopy coherent diagram, (by a second route).
          %h2#homotopy_groups_or_homotopy_progroups Homotopy groups or homotopy progroups?
          %p
            One obvious case to investigate of the above is to take a pointed space
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi n
                    %mi th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^th
            homotopy group functor
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n = [S^n, -]
            to the Čech or Vietoris complex to get a progroup,
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(\check{C}(X))
          %h3#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %strong
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^{th}
              Čech homotopy group
            of a pointed space
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is defined to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi lim
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \check{\pi_n}(\check{C}(X)) = lim \pi_n(\check{C}(X))
          %h3#examples Examples
          %p
            If
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is compact metric then it has countable cofinal subcategories of covers, so the progroups
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(\check{C}(X))
            can be replaced up to isomorphism by inverse sequences, indexed by the natural numbers. (These are sometimes called
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em towers
          %p Here are two specific examples:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Warsaw+circle"} Warsaw circle
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_W
                %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(\check{C}(S_W))
                is isomorphic to the constant tower with value
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\infty
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed ":" do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    dyadic solenoid
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/dyadic+solenoid"} ?
                %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Pro
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Groups
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pro(Groups)
                to the inverse sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi a
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\infty\stackrel{a}{\leftarrow} C_\infty\stackrel{a}{\leftarrow}C_\infty\stackrel{a}{\leftarrow}C_\infty\stackrel{a}{\leftarrow}C_\infty\stackrel{a}{\leftarrow}\ldots
          %p
            where if
            %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is the generator of
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f0fb655cf193ca709f3ce8e7497e67ab44ac03f4_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(c) = c^2
          %p This second example is certainly not isomorphic to a constant one. Note that it has trivial limit group, so is it possible to get some ‘useful’ limiting information from the progroup by taking some other type of ‘limiting’ approach? Yes. There are two related ways.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong>
                  The
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    derived functors of lim
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/derived+functors+of+lim"} ?
                \. Applied to the above progroup you get a definite measure of the non-triviality of the progroup. (This example is in that entry.)
            %li
              %p
                (A second method will be put here but will need additional work over on
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+homotopy+theory"} proper homotopy theory
          .query
            %p That is a start on it anyhow!
